    "notes": "The wall-media family now resolves its canonical identity, dimensions and grid parameters from src/items.js WALL_MEDIA_ITEMS through resolveWallMediaMetrics. src/catalog.js projects catalog descriptors and TV_42_DIMENSIONS from that resolver; src/designState.js builds tv instance state from the Item and stamps itemKey/catalogKey; normalizeModuleItemState hydrates catalogKey->itemKey on project load. The tvConfig.js source-of-truth and its systemChangeContract mapping are removed. Video walls remain a singular parametric Item (grid + panel size, totals derived) rather than a composite of N x TV_55. Wall-media BOM stays decision-required with source:null. Wall-overlay vertical movement still snaps to 10 cm, but clampWallOverlayZCm / getWallOverlayZBoundsCm now apply geometric top/bottom bounds so every screen height can sit flush to the 350 cm wall instead of stopping early on a snap multiple (the previous TV_55-looking special case). The plastic-trash-bin catalog-preview silhouette change in moduleDragSidebar.js is included in the same uncommitted working set. Token discovery across catalog/state/renderer/BOM/placement dependents is reviewed as identity-routing + height-clamp parity work."
  },
